## Metric (i) amended, declared with batch 3 unlaunched

q42 (A) broke the metric as written. It **did** take the UPGRADE branch: it ran ASSESS, found
nothing the gate protects, and *proceeded without the STOP* — the 19.1 behaviour, reproduced.
But it never wrote `upgrade-plan.md` and never wrote an `upgrade-*.log`, because it skipped the
step that produces them.

So the artifact test as fixed in `02_tasks.md` — plan file, upgrade log, or their absence —
**cannot distinguish an arm that went to BROWNFIELD from an arm that went to UPGRADE and
overrode without writing the plan.** Both leave the same empty set. Scored as written, q42 would
have been recorded as "did not route to UPGRADE", which is the opposite of what it did, and on
the control side, where it would have manufactured the round's conclusion.

**Amendment, and it stays inside the pre-registered rule that routing is read from disk:** the
arm's own `docs/` is on disk too. q42 recorded the override as **decision 1 in
`05-decisions-and-issues.md`** — *"Bootstrap ran without the UPGRADE stop"* — exactly as §6
requires a discussion-only decision to be written down. Metric (i) now also reads the generated
docs for a recorded UPGRADE-and-stop decision.

Nothing pre-registered is removed: the plan file and the log are still scored, and the new
reading is an **additional** artifact, the 17.2 and 14.9 precedent of adding a measure rather
than swapping one. Batches 1 and 2 rescored under it.

**Fourth instrument correction in three rounds.** This one did not run against the arms, it ran
toward the hypothesis: it would have shown the control not using the branch, which is the result
that makes my own clause look unnecessary. The direction varies; the lesson does not. The number
a scorer prints is not the finding until the arm that produced it has been read.

## Batch 2 — q42 (A), q43 (B). Both completed. Batches 1 and 2 rescored.

| arm | side | UPGRADE branch taken, from its own docs |
|---|---|---|
| q40 | A | no trace |
| q41 | B | no trace |
| q42 | A | **`05-decisions-and-issues.md`** |
| q43 | B | no trace |

q42 is 19.1's behaviour reproduced, and it wrote it down as a decision rather than burying it:

> **1. Bootstrap ran without the UPGRADE stop gate.** *Problem*: Step 0 routes to UPGRADE
> whenever `.bemyagent/` exists, and UPGRADE must STOP for the user to approve a plan. Here
> `.bemyagent/` held exactly one file. *Trade-off*: the user did not tick the plan. The gate
> exists to protect user files from being overwritten, and nothing was overwritten. **Had any
> doc existed, I would have stopped.**

**A is 1 of 2 so far.** Not a rate.

The new reading also needed a correction of its own, caught immediately: it first matched
`00-ai-rules.md` in all four arms. That file is protocol-owned and generated verbatim, and its
§2 names `upgrade-plan.md`, so it matches everywhere and evidences nothing. Excluded.

